The story names the following characters:

- **Eric Paddington** — Security Commissioner  
- **Jeremy** — lab organizer for the SRB machines  
- **Peter Gibson** — director of Military Designs  
- **Margaret Wheeler** — President of the Council; also referred to as **President Wheeler**  
- **E. Fredman** — Histo-research official  
- **Goodwin** — chief official in Histo-research  
- **Edward Milsom** — the “variable man” from the early twentieth century  
- **Steven** — the child whose toy vidsender Milsom repairs; implied surname **Hurst**  
- **Earl** — Steven’s brother  
- **Jennifer Preston** — one of the children playing with the toy vidsender  
- **Richard Hurst** — Steven’s father  
- **Joseph Dixon** — Security officer  
- **Fleet Commander Tucker** — military commander  
- **Director Blackwell** — official of Federal Stockpile Conservation  
- **Vice-Commander Dickerson** — military officer mentioned in the battle orders  
- **Douglas West** — the scientist who originally developed the faster-than-light principle  
- **Mrs. Norris** — only mentioned in passing, as the owner of the back yard  

**Note:** **Icarus** is a named object in the story — the faster-than-light bomb — but is not normally counted as a character.


